 "short_name": "Enoch Mgijima",
 "_doc": "'Solar' print-stream statement (same engine as Breede Valley / Naledi / Bitou: 'Account date', 'Receipts posted to', a 'Service Type / Tariff / Consumption / Basic' summary) but the text layer interleaves the left message column with the summary, so rows are matched mid-line, never line-anchored. Electricity is ONE summary row 'ELECTRICITY CONSUMPTION <tariff> <kWh> <basic> <amount incl VAT>'; no meter number, readings or dates are printed. Only property rates (zero-rated) sit beside it, so the statement's TOTAL VAT is the electricity VAT: total_ex_vat_r = amount - TOTAL VAT, other_r = the printed basic, standard_r = the rest (assumes the basic column is ex VAT). The 'Cpy VAT No' on the bill is Telkom's (customer) - NOT used; FINGERPRINT is the municipality's 'Registration No' as printed + its name. IDENTITY: only circular is possible (no electricity sub-total); the independent sanity is TOTAL VAT = 15/115 of the amount (holds to the cent on every bill), run as identity on the circular eno_elec_ex_r. One statement is a credit-only month with no electricity line (routes, no row). Checked on 10 bills.",
